{"name":"In the Tropics","hex":"#a3bc3a","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"tropics","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["plural of tropic"]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The region of the Earth centred on the equator and lying between the Tropic of Cancer and the Tropic of Capricorn and characterized by a hot climate."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tropics"}],"entries":[{"title":"Tropics","blocks":[{"text":"The tropics are the region of Earth surrounding the equator, where the Sun may shine directly overhead. This contrasts with the temperate or polar regions of Earth, where the Sun can never be directly overhead. Because of Earth's axial tilt, the width of the tropics is twice the tilt. The tropics are also referred to as the tropical zone and the torrid zone."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b0/World_map_indicating_tropics_and_subtropics.png/330px-World_map_indicating_tropics_and_subtropics.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tropics","wikidata":"Q42530"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2c/Bora_Bora.jpg/500px-Bora_Bora.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2c/Bora_Bora.jpg/500px-Bora_Bora.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Aerial view of Bora Bora in French Polynesia","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABora_Bora.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1c/Kota_Kinabalu_by_Dale_Preston.jpg/500px-Kota_Kinabalu_by_Dale_Preston.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1c/Kota_Kinabalu_by_Dale_Preston.jpg/1280px-Kota_Kinabalu_by_Dale_Preston.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&u